You can also stream the R output --- not sure if you can
turn off saving it in memory, though --- the doc for rstan::stan()
says you can supply a sample file, but doesn't say anything about
turning off the in-memory saves.

It's possible to run in CmdStan and then read the results back
into RStan.  And rstan::stan_dump() can write your data in a format
that is readable by CmdStan.

