On Wednesday, July 15, 2015 at 5:36:00 PM UTC-4, Tim wrote:
> Is it possible to call Stan distribution from R, e.g. using Rcpp as a proxy?

Yes

> Are there any examples of this that can be found online?

No because it does not officially exist yet. If you can wait a few days for RStan 2.7.0, then skip step 1
Download https://raw.githubusercontent.com/stan-dev/rstan/develop/rstan/rstan/R/expose_stan_functions.R to your working directory and comment out the line toward the end that says "#include <src/stan/lang/rethrow_located.hpp>"
Write a .stan function like this:
functions {
  real foo_log(/* arguments, see chapter of user manual on User-Defined Functions */) {
    return(normal_log(y, 0, 1)); // for example
  }
}
model {}
Source the aforementioned expose_stan_functions.R file, call expose_stan_functions(), and then call foo_log() from R with whatever arguments it takes.

Ben

