Glad to help. And logistic regressions (and GLMs in general) will be much much simpler to fit using Stan soon. We have an R package almost ready that will allow you to write this is R

stan_glm(y ~ X1 + X2, family = binomial)

it will use Stan to fit the model without even having to compile any c++ code when you run it. All the techniques for performance boosts that we can do automatically will be implemented behind the scenes. You also won't have to worry about the log-likelihood computations as this will be done too. We'll post updates when it's available to try out.

