On Tuesday, July 21, 2015 at 2:21:27 AM UTC-4, Sebastian Weber wrote:
> How about making pairs plots of the respective (automatically transformed) unconstrained parameter? Would that be doable?

There is a function to return all the unconstrained parameters, but RStan doesn't know the names or the dimensions of the unconstrained parameters. Also, in the case of a simplex, there are fewer unconstrained parameters than constrained parameters. So, pairs() wouldn't know what an unconstrained, e.g., "theta" refers to.

