On Friday, July 24, 2015 at 9:52:53 AM UTC-4, Sebastian Weber wrote:
> However, I did have in mind to deploy my own library, which uses some stan models behind the scenes to do its work. So from what I get from you, is that I could for example setup a script which compiles my model like
>
> stan_model <- stan("my_internal_library_model.stan", chains=0)

The rstan 2.7.0 package looks for a serialized stanmodel object next to the .stan file, not a stanfit object. So, you want to call stan_model() on a .stan file with auto_write = TRUE, and that does a saveRDS().

Ben

