How hard would it be to replace?  Here's their code:

http://eigen.tuxfamily.org/dox/unsupported/MatrixExponential_8h_source.html

Is the problem these floating-point only methods?

  119     void computeUV(double);
  120
  125     void computeUV(float);
  126
  131     void computeUV(long double);

They're defined later in the file and look like it might be possible to
code them, but they depend on this crazy function std::frexp() that grabs
the exponent and manitssa of a floating point.  That's not going to play
nicely with autodiff, is it?

It also depends on this file, which seems suboptimal:

http://eigen.tuxfamily.org/dox/unsupported/StemFunction_8h_source.html

but we could easily specialize.

- Bob

