Although this is slipping out of the scope of the mailing list, I'd like to add that although a spatiotemporal model for a signal on the sphere is straightforward, I don't see such a simple GP model useful for EEG analysis. (I have done EEG/ERP in the past.) Maybe GP's would make more sense in a more complicated model, though. (Like having a spectral decomposition, or something. The spatial variation is after a convolution, and models that decompose or deconvolve are more useful than smoothing models there.)

