> 3) Without the scatter (a two medium mixture model) everything works out, but I have the (minor) problem that the mus/sigmas contain both the low and high values. This is not really important, but this screws up my HDI (high density interval) calculations. Is there another way to prevent this than constraining the priors ?

Nope --- that's the only way other than post-processing.

