If you can express the system in discrete time as a linear dynamic model you can use a forward pass of the Kalman filter to calculate the log-likelihood marginalizing over the latent variables. You can find my various attempts at implementing this here: https://github.com/jrnold/ssmodels-in-stan.  I apologize in advance for the code being a bit of a mess; I've been meaning to clean it up for external consumption for a while. But despite the mess, it still may be better than starting from scratch.

